1. Platform concept
Build one system around a single miner identity that follows each ASIC from intake → test → repair → inventory → field deployment → client billing/revenue → retirement.

Core idea:

Every miner gets a CT Miner ID.
That CT ID links together:

Serial number

MAC address

Control board ID

Hashboard IDs if available

Client owner

Rack/shelf/bin location

Worker name

Pool/subaccount

Test history

Repair history

Parts used

Field deployment history

Revenue and hashrate history

Photos/logs/firmware/config snapshots

2. Physical layout
A. Intake / onboarding station
Purpose: receive miner, identify it, test it, label it, and decide where it goes.

Suggested station equipment:

240V/208V test power with metered PDU

Network switch with isolated onboarding VLAN

Barcode scanner

QR code / thermal label printer

Small receipt/sticker printer for rack tags

Operator touchscreen or rugged tablet

Status light tower: pass / fail / testing / needs review

Camera for intake photo

Scale optional

Airflow duct or test fan shroud

Sound/temperature sensors optional

“Known good” test pool credentials

Workflow:

Operator scans vendor serial or existing barcode.

System checks if miner already exists.

If new, create CT Miner ID.

Print CT asset label.

Plug miner into onboarding switch and power.

System detects MAC/IP.

System verifies miner model, firmware, hostname, pool settings, hashrate, fans, temps, hashboards.

System flashes shelf LED or shows IP/rack position.

System prints final status label:

PASSED — ready for deployment

REPAIR — send to bench

PARTS — not economical

QUARANTINE — identity mismatch

B. Repair diagnostic bench
Purpose: deeper troubleshooting and repair logging.

Suggested labels:

RB-01 Repair Bench 1

RB-02 Repair Bench 2

TRIAGE-RACK

FAILED-HASHBOARD

FAILED-CONTROL

FAILED-PSU

AWAITING-PARTS

POST-REPAIR-TEST

Workflow:

Operator scans miner QR.

GUI opens full history.

Operator selects issue category:

No boot

No network

Low hashrate

Missing hashboard

High temp

Fan issue

PSU issue

Firmware/config issue

System pulls logs and compares against previous tests.

Operator logs repair attempt.

Parts are scanned out of inventory.

Time starts/stops automatically or manually.

Miner is retested.

Outcome:

Pass → service rack

Fail → second repair attempt

Scrap/parts → parts rack

Escalate → senior tech review

