4. Core workflows
Workflow 1 — new miner intake
Receive miner
→ scan serial
→ create CT Miner ID
→ print asset label
→ plug into test station
→ auto-detect IP/MAC
→ verify model/firmware
→ apply test pool config
→ run 15–60 minute burn-in test
→ collect logs/metrics
→ pass/fail decision
→ print destination label
Pass criteria example:

Hashrate within 90–95% of expected model rate

All hashboards detected

Fans healthy

Temps within limit

Pool accepted shares

No abnormal hardware error rate

MAC matches recorded asset

Worker config correct

Stable for required test duration

Workflow 2 — failed onboarding
Failed intake
→ assign fault code
→ print repair ticket
→ move to repair rack
→ scan into repair bench
→ diagnose
→ parts/time logged
→ retest
→ pass, retry, or scrap
Workflow 3 — repair bench
Scan CT Miner ID
→ load history
→ guided diagnostic checklist
→ pull logs
→ compare to baseline
→ operator records issue
→ system suggests likely fixes
→ scan parts used
→ retest
→ close repair order
Workflow 4 — field deployment
Service-ready miner
→ assign to client/site/rack/slot
→ print deployment label
→ scan at truck/loadout
→ scan at site gateway
→ scan into exact rack slot
→ gateway verifies MAC/IP/worker
→ miner begins production
→ portal starts tracking revenue/performance
Workflow 5 — field service
Gateway flags issue
→ ticket created
→ operator receives iOS task
→ app guides field fix
→ scan miner/rack
→ confirm issue
→ replace fan/config/reboot if simple
→ retest
→ close ticket or mark remove-to-repair
Workflow 6 — remove from field
Operator scans miner
→ status: removed from production
→ reason selected
→ replacement miner scanned in
→ revenue tracking switches to replacement
→ failed miner routed to repair station
